# Per-lens tune for the AI exposure/color system.
# Read by the firmware (modules/ettr/ai_lut.h -> ai_lens_tune_load) whenever
# the mounted lens changes while the AI is active.
#
# Format:  lens_id|contrast|saturation|color_tone[|ev_bias|wb_r|wb_b[|ca_strength|fringe_reduce]]
#   lens_id       Canon lens id (see ML: lens_info.lens_id; also logged as
#                 Lens= in unified_log.txt). lens_id 0 = DEFAULT for any
#                 unlisted lens.
#   contrast      -4..4   picture-style offsets, JPEG only -- applied when the
#   saturation    -4..4   "AI Picture Tune" menu toggle is ON
#   color_tone    -4..4
#   ev_bias       optional, 1/8 EV added to the ETTR exposure target (RAW).
#                 Negative = protect highlights: -8 meters this lens 1 EV
#                 lower. Range -24..8. Applied whenever AI modes cover the
#                 current shooting mode.
#   wb_r, wb_b    optional AI White Balance trims, 1024 = 1.0x (only active
#                 with "AI White Balance" ON). Suppression scale: wb_r < 1024
#                 warms (more red), wb_b > 1024 warms (less blue).
#   ca_strength   optional, [0..100] chromatic aberration correction strength,
#                 sourced by ai_sidecar_write()'s lens block (Component 5).
#                 Must stay identical to the StudioRoom app/src/main/assets/
#                 ml/lens_tune.tbl copy for any lens_id present in both files
#                 (spec cr2-intelligence-integration, Requirement 3.4).
#   fringe_reduce optional, [0..100] purple/green fringe suppression strength.
#
# Old 4/6-column rows stay valid (no exposure/WB/CA change; CA defaults 0/0).
#
# lens_id 0 = default (neutral).
0|0|0|0|0|1024|1024|0|0
# Tamron SP AF 20-40mm f/2.7-3.5 Aspherical (IF) -- reports id 160, "21-39mm".
# Blooms highlights (~+1 EV vs metered target, IMG_5296-5299 2026-07-19):
# ev -8 = meter 1 EV more protective (kept). CA values mirrored from the
# StudioRoom asset copy (shared lens_id, Requirement 3.4) -- kept.
# WB trims + color_tone NEUTRALIZED 2026-07-21: the earlier warm bias
# (wb_r 960 / wb_b 1152) + color_tone +1 were compounding a green/warm JPEG
# cast on top of the OVF one-shot-lag WB issue (see project-context.md).
# Reset to neutral so the base AI WB behavior can be judged without a per-lens
# color offset stacked on it. contrast -1 kept (tone preference, not a cast).
160|-1|0|0|-8|1024|1024|15|20  #user
# lens_id 228 is not present in the StudioRoom copy (no parity constraint);
# CA data not yet calibrated for this lens, default 0/0.
228|-1|0|0|0|1024|1024|0|0  #user
